IMPORT prelude

-- Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 (NSW), Part 4 (the Victims Support Scheme), with the Victims Rights and Support
-- Regulation 2019, which sets the numbers the Act leaves to it.
--
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE. The rules are written in the Act's own actors and terms: "the act", "a primary victim",
-- "a secondary victim", "a family victim", "a parent, step-parent or guardian who is caring for a child", "the
-- applicant", "the Commissioner". The victim's questions are in vrsa-seat.l4, which IMPORTs this module and restates
-- no rule.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Act: s 18 (injury, financial support), s 19 (act of violence), s 19A (act of modern slavery),
-- s 19AB (road crime), ss 20-22 (primary, secondary and family victims; immediate family), s 23 (eligibility), s 24
-- (death of victim), s 25 (persons not eligible), ss 26-29A (composition of support, with the cross-reductions in
-- ss 26(2) and 27(2)), s 30(2) (no assistance for loss already paid for), s 30A (each type of support once), ss 34-36
-- (recognition payment categories A-D, who receives category A, one payment per series), s 38 (who may apply), s 39
-- (documentary evidence), s 40 (time limits, and claims under an application), s 43(1), (4) (the application must be
-- determined, with written notice), s 47 (funeral and clean-up expenses of others), s 53 (recognition payment
-- suspended pending review), s 54(2) (payment of a claim). Regulation: cl 5 (counselling hours), cl 7 (ongoing
-- counselling for child victims of sexual assault or physical abuse), cl 8 (counsellor rates), cl 9 (as not covered),
-- cl 10-13 (financial assistance amounts), cl 14 (recognition payment amounts).
--
-- REGULATIVE RULES (DEONTIC): s 40(1)-(3), (5), (7) (the application must be duly made in time), s 43(1), (4) (the
-- Commissioner must determine it and give written notice), s 40(6) with s 54(2) (claims under the application, and
-- payment).
--
-- EDITION. Act: act-2013-037, corpus document nsw_legislation:2025-02-01/act-2013-037. Regulation: sl-2019-0398,
-- corpus document nsw_legislation:2025-02-01/sl-2019-0398. Both from the Open Australian Legal Corpus (version 7.1.0,
-- NSW Legislation collected 10 March 2025), deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/act-2013-037.txt and
-- ../../../victims-rights-and-support-regulation-2019/registers/source-bundle/sl-2019-0398.txt.
-- NOT THE CURRENT OFFICIAL TEXT; IT MAY BE OUT OF DATE. The amounts are those fixed in the deposited Regulation.
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0).
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Victims Rights and Support Act 2013 (NSW) -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `What this encoding does not cover`

-- The stable l4 has no REFUSE. A rule that reaches a gap answers with the reason, and a test asserts it.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- Reg cl 9: "financial assistance for actual loss of earnings is to be calculated at the rate of weekly payment of
    -- compensation payable under section 37 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987 (as in force immediately before its
    -- substitution by the Workers Compensation Legislation Amendment Act 2012) and indexed in accordance with law."
    `the cl 9 rate: s 37 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987 as in force before the 2012 amendments, and its indexed amounts, are not deposited`

§§ `Dates`

-- The clock is days. Periods "within 2 years after" a day end on the same day and month that many years later.
-- READING: the Interpretation Act 1987 (not deposited) governs how periods are counted; 29 February, in a year with
-- no 29 February, becomes 28 February.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` `the year` IF
        `the year` MODULO 4 EQUALS 0
    AND (   (NOT (`the year` MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))
         OR `the year` MODULO 400 EQUALS 0)

GIVEN `years`   IS A NUMBER
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`years` `years after` `the day` MEANS
    IF      DATE_DAY `the day` EQUALS 29
        AND DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 2
        AND (NOT (`is a leap year` (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS `years`)))
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS `years`)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS `years`)

GIVEN `the first`  IS A DATE
      `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is on or before` `the first` `the second` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second`

GIVEN `the first`  IS A DATE
      `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first` `and` `the second` MEANS
    IF `is on or before` `the second` `the first`
    THEN `the first`
    ELSE `the second`

GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
      `the end`   IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- "a child" and "turns 18 years of age" (s 40(1), (5)); s 21(2)(b) "under the age of 18 years".
`the age of majority` MEANS 18

GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the person turns 18` `the date of birth` MEANS
    `the age of majority` `years after` `the date of birth`

GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day`           IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `was a child on` `the date of birth` `the day` IF
    NOT (`is on or before` (`the day the person turns 18` `the date of birth`) `the day`)

§§ `The Regulation's amounts`

-- Reg cl 10 (primary victims), for s 26(1)(b), (c) of the Act.
`cl 10(1) -- maximum for a primary victim's immediate needs`                     MEANS 5000
`cl 10(2) -- maximum for a primary victim's economic loss`                       MEANS 30000
`cl 10(3)(a) -- limit for actual loss of earnings`                               MEANS 20000
`cl 10(3)(b) -- limit for out-of-pocket expenses`                                MEANS 5000
`cl 10(3)(d) -- limit for justice related expenses`                              MEANS 5000
`cl 10(3)(e) -- limit for clothing and personal effects`                         MEANS 1500

-- Reg cl 11 (parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child primary victim), for s 27(1).
`cl 11(1) -- maximum for a carer's economic loss`                                MEANS 30000
`cl 11(2)(a) -- limit for a carer's actual loss of earnings`                     MEANS 20000
`cl 11(2)(b) -- limit for a carer's out-of-pocket expenses`                      MEANS 5000
`cl 11(2)(d) -- limit for a carer's justice related expenses`                    MEANS 5000
`cl 11(2)(e) -- limit for the child's clothing and personal effects`             MEANS 1500

-- Reg cl 12 (family victims), for s 29(1)(b), (c), (d).
`cl 12(1) -- maximum for a family victim's immediate needs`                      MEANS 5000
`cl 12(2) -- maximum for funeral expenses, in total`                             MEANS 9500
`cl 12(3) -- maximum for a family victim's justice related expenses`             MEANS 5000

-- Reg cl 13 (persons other than family victims), for s 47(3).
`cl 13(a) -- maximum for immediate needs under s 47`                             MEANS 5000
`cl 13(b) -- maximum for funeral expenses under s 47`                            MEANS 9500

-- Reg cl 14 (recognition payments), for s 36.
`cl 14(a) -- category A under s 36(1)(a)`                                        MEANS 15000
`cl 14(b) -- category A under s 36(1)(b)`                                        MEANS 7500
`cl 14(c) -- category B`                                                         MEANS 10000
`cl 14(d) -- category C`                                                         MEANS 5000
`cl 14(e) -- category D`                                                         MEANS 1500

-- Reg cl 5 and cl 8 (approved counselling services), for ss 32, 33.
`cl 5(2) -- hours of counselling`                                                MEANS 22
`cl 5(3) -- initial hours while victim status is established`                    MEANS 2
`cl 5(5) -- dollar limit for counselling outside Australia`                      MEANS 5500
`cl 8(2) -- travel period that counts, more than this many hours`                MEANS 2
`cl 8(3) -- GST cap, as a share of the scale amount`                             MEANS 10%

-- The Act's own periods (s 40).
`s 40(1) -- years to apply`                                                      MEANS 2
`s 40(3) -- years to apply after the cause of death is established`              MEANS 2
`s 40(5) -- years to apply for a recognition payment`                            MEANS 10
`s 40(6)(a) -- years in which claims may be made under an application`           MEANS 5

§ `Part 4 Division 1 -- the act and the victims (ss 18 to 22)`

§§ `ss 19, 19A, 19AB -- act of violence, act of modern slavery, road crime`

-- One case is one act (s 19(7) and s 19A(6): a series of related acts "constitutes a single act").
DECLARE `The act` HAS
    -- s 19(1)(a), (2): "has apparently occurred in the course of the commission of an offence" (including conduct
    -- that would be an offence but for the person's age or mental illness or impairment).
    `apparently occurred in the course of the commission of an offence`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 19(1)(b), (3): "has involved violent conduct against one or more persons"; violent conduct "extends to sexual
    -- assault and domestic violence" (defined in s 19(8)).
    `involved violent conduct against one or more persons`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 19(1)(c): "has resulted in injury or death to one or more of those persons". s 18: injury "means actual bodily
    -- harm, grievous bodily harm or psychological or psychiatric harm but does not include injury arising from loss or
    -- damage to property".
    `resulted in injury or death to one or more of those persons`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 19A(1), s 19AB(1)(a): "committed in New South Wales". s 19 states no place (finding 1).
    `was committed in New South Wales`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 19A(1)(a): "apparently occurred in the course of commission of an offence or other conduct constituting modern
    -- slavery within the meaning of the Modern Slavery Act 2018" (borrowed: a fact).
    `apparently occurred in the course of an offence or other conduct constituting modern slavery` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 19A(1)(b): "subjecting one or more persons to any form of slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child within
    -- the meaning of section 93AB of the Crimes Act 1900" (borrowed: a fact).
    `involved subjecting one or more persons to slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 19A(1)(c): "has resulted in injury or death to one of those persons".
    `resulted in injury or death to one of the persons subjected to it`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 19AB(1)(a): "(i) involved a motor vehicle, and (ii) caused the death of another person".
    `involved a motor vehicle and caused the death of another person`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 19AB(1)(b)(i): "charges have been laid against the alleged offender for an offence in relation to the act".
    `charges have been laid against the alleged offender`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 19AB(1)(b)(ii): "charges cannot be laid because the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified but, on
    -- the balance of probabilities, an offence has apparently occurred". (b)(iii), circumstances prescribed by the
    -- regulations: the deposited Regulation prescribes none.
    `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, and an offence has apparently occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 25(2): "took the form of, or the injury arose as a consequence of, a motor accident within the meaning of the
    -- Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999" (borrowed: a fact).
    `took the form of, or the injury arose from, a motor accident`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 25(2A)(a), (b).
    `took the form of the intentional killing of the primary victim`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `a person has been charged with murder in relation to the death`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 25(2B): "a terrorist act within the meaning of the Terrorism (Police Powers) Act 2002" (borrowed: a fact).
    `was a terrorist act`                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 25(2A): "(a) the act of violence took the form of the intentional killing of the primary victim, and (b) a person
-- has been charged with murder in relation to the death of the primary victim."
GIVEN `the act` IS A `The act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 25(2A) circumstances apply to` `the act` IF
        `the act`'s `took the form of the intentional killing of the primary victim`
    AND `the act`'s `a person has been charged with murder in relation to the death`

-- s 19AB(1): a road crime is (a) an act committed in NSW that involved a motor vehicle and caused the death of another
-- person, and (b) one for which charges have been laid, or cannot be laid because the alleged offender has died or
-- cannot be identified but an offence has apparently occurred.
GIVEN `the act` IS A `The act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a road crime` `the act` IF
        `the act`'s `was committed in New South Wales`
    AND `the act`'s `involved a motor vehicle and caused the death of another person`
    AND (   `the act`'s `charges have been laid against the alleged offender`
         OR `the act`'s `the alleged offender has died or cannot be identified, and an offence has apparently occurred`)

-- s 19(1): (a) and (b) and (c). s 19(3A): "a road crime is not an act of violence except in the circumstances provided
-- for in section 25(2A) and (2B)".
GIVEN `the act` IS A `The act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an act of violence` `the act` IF
        `the act`'s `apparently occurred in the course of the commission of an offence`
    AND `the act`'s `involved violent conduct against one or more persons`
    AND `the act`'s `resulted in injury or death to one or more of those persons`
    AND (   (NOT (`is a road crime` `the act`))
         OR `the s 25(2A) circumstances apply to` `the act`
         OR `the act`'s `was a terrorist act`)

-- s 19A(1): committed in NSW, and (a) and (b) and (c).
GIVEN `the act` IS A `The act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an act of modern slavery` `the act` IF
        `the act`'s `was committed in New South Wales`
    AND `the act`'s `apparently occurred in the course of an offence or other conduct constituting modern slavery`
    AND `the act`'s `involved subjecting one or more persons to slavery, servitude or forced labour of a child`
    AND `the act`'s `resulted in injury or death to one of the persons subjected to it`

DECLARE `Kind of act` IS ONE OF
    `an act of violence (s 19)`
    `an act of modern slavery (s 19A)`
    `a road crime (s 19AB)`

GIVEN `the act` IS A `The act`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Kind of act`
`the kinds of` `the act` MEANS
    concat (LIST (IF `is an act of violence` `the act` THEN LIST `an act of violence (s 19)` ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF `is an act of modern slavery` `the act` THEN LIST `an act of modern slavery (s 19A)` ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF `is a road crime` `the act` THEN LIST `a road crime (s 19AB)` ELSE EMPTY))

-- s 30A(1): "This section applies if an act is 2 or more of" an act of violence, an act of modern slavery, a road
-- crime. (2): "A victim is eligible for each type of support under the Scheme only once in relation to the act."
-- The encoding works out each class of victim once for the act, whatever its kinds, and lists counselling once.
GIVEN `the act` IS A `The act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30A applies to` `the act` IF
    count (`the kinds of` `the act`) AT LEAST 2

§§ `ss 20 to 22 -- primary, secondary and family victims`

-- s 22(3): "A member of the immediate family of a primary victim or a person who dies as a result of a road crime is
-- (a) the victim's or person's spouse, or (b) the victim's or person's de facto partner who has cohabited with the
-- victim or person for at least 2 years, or (c) a parent, guardian or step-parent of the victim or person, or (d) a
-- child or step-child of the victim or person or some other child of whom the victim or person is the guardian, or (e)
-- a brother, sister, half-brother, half-sister, step-brother or step-sister of the victim or person."
-- The relationship is that of the person to the one who died. "De facto partner": Interpretation Act s 21C (borrowed).
DECLARE `Relationship to the person who died` IS ONE OF
    `spouse`
    `de facto partner`
    `parent, guardian or step-parent`
    `child`
    `step-child, or a child of whom the person who died was the guardian`
    `brother, sister, half-brother, half-sister, step-brother or step-sister`
    `another relative`
    `no family relationship`

GIVEN `the relationship`                       IS A `Relationship to the person who died`
      `cohabited for at least 2 years`         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a member of the immediate family (s 22(3))` `the relationship` `cohabited for at least 2 years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relationship`
    WHEN `spouse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `de facto partner` THEN `cohabited for at least 2 years`
    WHEN `parent, guardian or step-parent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `child` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `step-child, or a child of whom the person who died was the guardian` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `brother, sister, half-brother, half-sister, step-brother or step-sister` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- One person, and what the act did to them. Facts for ss 20-25.
DECLARE `The person` HAS
    -- s 20(1): "a person who is injured, or dies, as a direct result of that act".
    `was injured as a direct result of the act`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 20(2): injured or dies as a direct result of "(a) trying to prevent another person from committing that act,
    -- or (b) trying to help or rescue another person against whom that act is being committed or has just been
    -- committed, or (c) trying to arrest another person who is committing, or who has just committed, that act".
    `was injured trying to prevent the act, help or rescue a person, or arrest the offender`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 21(1): "injured as a direct result of witnessing the act of violence that resulted in the injury to, or death
    -- of, the primary victim of that act". s 21(3): a primary victim here excludes one "only because of" s 20(2); the
    -- persons against whom the violent conduct was directed (s 19(1)(c)) are primary victims under s 20(1), so the
    -- act of violence itself supplies the primary victim.
    `was injured as a direct result of witnessing the act`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 21(2): injured "as a direct result of subsequently becoming aware of the act of violence", but only if "(a)
    -- the person is the parent or guardian of the primary victim of that act, and (b) the primary victim was under the
    -- age of 18 years at the time of that act, and (c) the person did not commit that act".
    `was injured as a direct result of subsequently becoming aware of the act`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the parent or guardian of the primary victim`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the primary victim was under 18 at the time of the act`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `committed the act`                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 23(2): "A parent, step-parent or guardian who is caring for a child who is a primary victim".
    `is a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child who is a primary victim`         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 22(1): "a member of the immediate family of a primary victim of that act who has died as a direct result of
    -- that act"; (1A): "of a person who has died as a result of the road crime". Membership is "at the time" of the act.
    `a person died as a result of the act`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `relationship to the person who died`                                                     IS A `Relationship to the person who died`
    `had cohabited with the person who died for at least 2 years`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 25(3)(b), (3A).
    `the person who died is the alleged offender`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `is also a member of the immediate family of another person who died as a result of the road crime` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 24: "A primary victim who dies ceases to be eligible"; "A family victim who dies ceases to be eligible".
    -- For an application made on a victim's behalf.
    `the victim has died`                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 25(1): "has been paid, or is entitled to be paid, compensation awarded by a court in respect of that act under
    -- Part 6 or if the person's application for such compensation is pending".
    `has been paid, is entitled to, or has applied for court compensation under Part 6`       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 25(3)(a): "the act occurred while the person was engaged in behaviour constituting an offence".
    `was engaged in behaviour constituting an offence when the act occurred`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 25(4): "imprisoned as a convicted inmate ... (unless the person was imprisoned only because of the person's
    -- failure to pay a pecuniary penalty)".
    `was imprisoned as a convicted inmate when the act occurred`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 25(5), (6): a judgment left to the Commissioner, answered conditionally.
    `the Commissioner is satisfied that special circumstances justify an exception`           IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A `The person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a member of the immediate family of the person who died` `the person` IF
        `the person`'s `a person died as a result of the act`
    AND `is a member of the immediate family (s 22(3))` (`the person`'s `relationship to the person who died`) (`the person`'s `had cohabited with the person who died for at least 2 years`)

-- s 20: primary victim of an act of violence or act of modern slavery.
GIVEN `the act` IS A `The act`
      `the person` IS A `The person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a primary victim of` `the act` `the person` IF
        (`is an act of violence` `the act` OR `is an act of modern slavery` `the act`)
    AND (   `the person`'s `was injured as a direct result of the act`
         OR `the person`'s `was injured trying to prevent the act, help or rescue a person, or arrest the offender`)

-- s 21: secondary victim of an act of violence only.
GIVEN `the act` IS A `The act`
      `the person` IS A `The person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a secondary victim of` `the act` `the person` IF
        `is an act of violence` `the act`
    AND (   `the person`'s `was injured as a direct result of witnessing the act`
         OR (    `the person`'s `was injured as a direct result of subsequently becoming aware of the act`
             AND `the person`'s `is the parent or guardian of the primary victim`
             AND `the person`'s `the primary victim was under 18 at the time of the act`
             AND (NOT (`the person`'s `committed the act`))))

-- s 22(1): family victim of an act of violence (not of an act of modern slavery: finding 4).
GIVEN `the act` IS A `The act`
      `the person` IS A `The person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a family victim of the act of violence` `the act` `the person` IF
        `is an act of violence` `the act`
    AND `is a member of the immediate family of the person who died` `the person`

-- s 22(1A): family victim of a road crime.
GIVEN `the act` IS A `The act`
      `the person` IS A `The person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a family victim of the road crime` `the act` `the person` IF
        `is a road crime` `the act`
    AND `is a member of the immediate family of the person who died` `the person`

-- s 23(2): a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child who is a primary victim of an act of violence or act
-- of modern slavery.
GIVEN `the act` IS A `The act`
      `the person` IS A `The person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a carer of a child primary victim of` `the act` `the person` IF
        (`is an act of violence` `the act` OR `is an act of modern slavery` `the act`)
    AND `the person`'s `is a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child who is a primary victim`

§ `Part 4 Division 2 -- eligibility for support (ss 23 to 25)`

-- s 23(1)-(5): each class of victim, with the section that describes its support.
DECLARE `Victim class` IS ONE OF
    `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)`
    `a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child primary victim (s 23(2), s 27)`
    `a secondary victim (s 23(3), s 28)`
    `a family victim of an act of violence (s 23(4), s 29)`
    `a family victim of a road crime (s 23(5), s 29A)`

GIVEN `the act` IS A `The act`
      `the person` IS A `The person`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Victim class`
`the classes of victim of` `the act` `the person` MEANS
    concat (LIST (IF `is a primary victim of` `the act` `the person` THEN LIST `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)` ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF `is a carer of a child primary victim of` `the act` `the person` THEN LIST `a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child primary victim (s 23(2), s 27)` ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF `is a secondary victim of` `the act` `the person` THEN LIST `a secondary victim (s 23(3), s 28)` ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF `is a family victim of the act of violence` `the act` `the person` THEN LIST `a family victim of an act of violence (s 23(4), s 29)` ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF `is a family victim of the road crime` `the act` `the person` THEN LIST `a family victim of a road crime (s 23(5), s 29A)` ELSE EMPTY))

DECLARE `Reason not eligible` IS ONE OF
    `the victim has died: the victim ceases to be eligible, and a pending application does not survive (s 24)`
    `compensation awarded by a court under Part 6 has been paid, is payable or has been applied for (s 25(1))`
    `the act took the form of, or the injury arose from, a motor accident (s 25(2))`
    `the act occurred while the person was engaged in behaviour constituting an offence (s 25(3)(a))`
    `a family victim of the road crime only as a member of the alleged offender's immediate family (s 25(3)(b))`
    `a convicted inmate when the act occurred, unless the Commissioner is satisfied that special circumstances justify an exception (s 25(4), (5))`

-- Whether the class's support rests on an act of violence alone (s 25(2) and (3)(a) speak only of an act of violence).
GIVEN `the act`   IS A `The act`
      `the class` IS A `Victim class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`rests on an act of violence alone` `the act` `the class` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a secondary victim (s 23(3), s 28)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a family victim of an act of violence (s 23(4), s 29)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a family victim of a road crime (s 23(5), s 29A)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOT (`is an act of modern slavery` `the act`)

-- s 25(2): not eligible "if that act took the form of, or the injury arose as a consequence of, a motor accident";
-- (2A): "Despite subsection (2), a family victim is eligible" in the s 25(2A) circumstances; (2B): "a primary victim and a
-- family victim are eligible" for a terrorist act. Secondary victims and carers have no exception (finding 6).
GIVEN `the act`   IS A `The act`
      `the class` IS A `Victim class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the motor accident exclusion applies to` `the act` `the class` IF
        `rests on an act of violence alone` `the act` `the class`
    AND `the act`'s `took the form of, or the injury arose from, a motor accident`
    AND (NOT (    `the class` EQUALS `a family victim of an act of violence (s 23(4), s 29)`
              AND `the s 25(2A) circumstances apply to` `the act`))
    AND (NOT (    (   `the class` EQUALS `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)`
                   OR `the class` EQUALS `a family victim of an act of violence (s 23(4), s 29)`)
              AND `the act`'s `was a terrorist act`))

-- s 24, s 25, in the order of the text. NOTHING: the class is not excluded.
GIVEN `the class`  IS A `Victim class`
      `the act`    IS A `The act`
      `the person` IS A `The person`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Reason not eligible`
`the reason the person is not eligible as` `the class` `for` `the act` `the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF      `the person`'s `the victim has died`
            AND (   `the class` EQUALS `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)`
                 OR `the class` EQUALS `a family victim of an act of violence (s 23(4), s 29)`
                 OR `the class` EQUALS `a family victim of a road crime (s 23(5), s 29A)`)
        THEN JUST `the victim has died: the victim ceases to be eligible, and a pending application does not survive (s 24)`
        IF      (NOT (`the class` EQUALS `a family victim of a road crime (s 23(5), s 29A)`))
            AND `the person`'s `has been paid, is entitled to, or has applied for court compensation under Part 6`
        THEN JUST `compensation awarded by a court under Part 6 has been paid, is payable or has been applied for (s 25(1))`
        IF `the motor accident exclusion applies to` `the act` `the class`
        THEN JUST `the act took the form of, or the injury arose from, a motor accident (s 25(2))`
        IF      `rests on an act of violence alone` `the act` `the class`
            AND `the person`'s `was engaged in behaviour constituting an offence when the act occurred`
        THEN JUST `the act occurred while the person was engaged in behaviour constituting an offence (s 25(3)(a))`
        IF      `the class` EQUALS `a family victim of a road crime (s 23(5), s 29A)`
            AND `the person`'s `the person who died is the alleged offender`
            AND (NOT (`the person`'s `is also a member of the immediate family of another person who died as a result of the road crime`))
        THEN JUST `a family victim of the road crime only as a member of the alleged offender's immediate family (s 25(3)(b))`
        IF      (NOT (`the class` EQUALS `a family victim of a road crime (s 23(5), s 29A)`))
            AND `the person`'s `was imprisoned as a convicted inmate when the act occurred`
            AND (NOT (`the person`'s `the Commissioner is satisfied that special circumstances justify an exception`))
        THEN JUST `a convicted inmate when the act occurred, unless the Commissioner is satisfied that special circumstances justify an exception (s 25(4), (5))`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `Victim status` IS ONE OF
    `eligible as` HAS `the eligible class` IS A `Victim class`
    `not eligible as` HAS `the excluded class` IS A `Victim class`
                          `because`            IS A `Reason not eligible`
    `not a victim of an act of violence, an act of modern slavery or a road crime (ss 19 to 23)`

GIVEN `the class`  IS A `Victim class`
      `the act`    IS A `The act`
      `the person` IS A `The person`
GIVETH A `Victim status`
`the status as` `the class` `for` `the act` `the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reason the person is not eligible as` `the class` `for` `the act` `the person`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `eligible as` `the class`
    WHEN JUST `the reason` THEN `not eligible as` `the class` `the reason`

GIVEN `the act`    IS A `The act`
      `the person` IS A `The person`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Victim status`
`the victim statuses of` `the act` `the person` MEANS
    IF null (`the classes of victim of` `the act` `the person`)
    THEN LIST `not a victim of an act of violence, an act of modern slavery or a road crime (ss 19 to 23)`
    ELSE map (GIVEN `c` YIELD `the status as` `c` `for` `the act` `the person`) (`the classes of victim of` `the act` `the person`)

GIVEN `the act`    IS A `The act`
      `the person` IS A `The person`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Victim class`
`the eligible classes of` `the act` `the person` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN `c` YIELD isNothing (`the reason the person is not eligible as` `c` `for` `the act` `the person`))
           (`the classes of victim of` `the act` `the person`)

§ `Part 4 Division 3 -- composition of support (ss 26 to 30A)`

-- s 18: "financial support" is financial assistance for immediate needs (s 26(1)(b), 29(1)(b)), for economic loss
-- (s 26(1)(c), 27, 29(1)(d)) and funeral expenses (s 29(1)(c)). Each amount below is the most that may be given.
DECLARE `Support` IS ONE OF
    `approved counselling services (ss 26(1)(a), 28, 29(1)(a), 29A)`
    `financial assistance for immediate needs (s 26(1)(b)), up to` HAS `immediate needs dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `financial assistance for economic loss (s 26(1)(c)), up to` HAS `economic loss dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `a recognition payment, if one is payable for the act (s 26(1)(d))`
    `financial assistance for economic loss while caring for the child (s 27), up to` HAS `carer dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `financial assistance for immediate needs (s 29(1)(b)), up to` HAS `family immediate needs dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `funeral expenses (s 29(1)(c)), up to this total for all the family victims` HAS `funeral dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `financial assistance for justice related expenses (s 29(1)(d)), up to` HAS `justice dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `a category A recognition payment, if one is payable to the person (s 29(3))`

GIVEN `the class` IS A `Victim class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`comes with counselling` `the class` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child primary victim (s 23(2), s 27)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- ss 26-29A, without counselling, which is listed once (s 30A; Reg cl 5(1) sets one limit for each act).
GIVEN `the class` IS A `Victim class`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Support`
`the financial support and recognition for` `the class` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)` THEN
        LIST `financial assistance for immediate needs (s 26(1)(b)), up to` `cl 10(1) -- maximum for a primary victim's immediate needs`,
             `financial assistance for economic loss (s 26(1)(c)), up to` `cl 10(2) -- maximum for a primary victim's economic loss`,
             `a recognition payment, if one is payable for the act (s 26(1)(d))`
    WHEN `a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child primary victim (s 23(2), s 27)` THEN
        LIST `financial assistance for economic loss while caring for the child (s 27), up to` `cl 11(1) -- maximum for a carer's economic loss`
    WHEN `a secondary victim (s 23(3), s 28)` THEN EMPTY
    WHEN `a family victim of an act of violence (s 23(4), s 29)` THEN
        LIST `financial assistance for immediate needs (s 29(1)(b)), up to` `cl 12(1) -- maximum for a family victim's immediate needs`,
             `funeral expenses (s 29(1)(c)), up to this total for all the family victims` `cl 12(2) -- maximum for funeral expenses, in total`,
             `financial assistance for justice related expenses (s 29(1)(d)), up to` `cl 12(3) -- maximum for a family victim's justice related expenses`,
             `a category A recognition payment, if one is payable to the person (s 29(3))`
    WHEN `a family victim of a road crime (s 23(5), s 29A)` THEN EMPTY

GIVEN `the act`    IS A `The act`
      `the person` IS A `The person`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Support`
`the support for` `the act` `the person` MEANS
    append (IF any (GIVEN `c` YIELD `comes with counselling` `c`) (`the eligible classes of` `the act` `the person`)
            THEN LIST `approved counselling services (ss 26(1)(a), 28, 29(1)(a), 29A)`
            ELSE EMPTY)
           (concat (map (GIVEN `c` YIELD `the financial support and recognition for` `c`) (`the eligible classes of` `the act` `the person`)))

§§ `s 30(2) -- loss already paid for`

-- s 30(2): "Financial assistance is not payable ... to the extent that the victim, parent, step-parent or guardian has
-- received, or is entitled to receive, payment for that loss arising from that act ... under any insurance or
-- agreement or arrangement under any other Act or law." Each head of loss is taken net of what is paid for it.
DECLARE `Expense` HAS
    `amount`                              IS A NUMBER
    `paid or payable from another source` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the expense` IS AN `Expense`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part not paid from another source` `the expense` MEANS
    max 0 (`the expense`'s `amount` MINUS `the expense`'s `paid or payable from another source`)

§§ `s 26, Reg cl 10 -- a primary victim's financial assistance`

DECLARE `Primary victim claim` HAS
    -- s 26(1)(b): "expenses for treatment or other measures that need to be taken urgently, as a direct result of that
    -- act ..., to secure the victim's safety, health or well being".
    `immediate needs expenses`                                       IS AN `Expense`
    -- cl 10(3)(a), (b): whether "the victim can demonstrate actual loss of earnings".
    `can demonstrate actual loss of earnings`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 9: the weekly rate, not computable from the deposit (see `Why not covered`), so an input.
    `weekly rate of actual loss of earnings under cl 9`              IS A NUMBER
    `weeks of actual loss of earnings`                               IS A NUMBER
    `lost earnings paid or payable from another source`              IS A NUMBER
    `out-of-pocket expenses`                                         IS AN `Expense`
    -- cl 10(3)(c): "other than expenses for which financial assistance for immediate needs is available".
    `medical and dental expenses not claimed as immediate needs`     IS AN `Expense`
    -- cl 10(3)(d): "expenses associated with criminal or coronial proceedings ..., making statements to police,
    -- preparing victim impact statements and similar justice related expenses".
    `justice related expenses`                                       IS AN `Expense`
    -- cl 10(3)(e): "loss of, or damage to, clothing or other personal effects worn or carried by the primary victim at
    -- the time of the act".
    `clothing and personal effects`                                  IS AN `Expense`
    -- s 26(2).
    `paid or approved to the parent, step-parent or guardian under s 27` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Financial assistance` HAS
    `for immediate needs`                     IS A NUMBER
    `for actual loss of earnings`             IS A NUMBER
    `for out-of-pocket expenses`              IS A NUMBER
    `for medical and dental expenses`         IS A NUMBER
    `for justice related expenses`            IS A NUMBER
    `for clothing and personal effects`       IS A NUMBER
    `for economic loss, within the maximum`   IS A NUMBER
    `taken off under s 26(2) or s 27(2)`      IS A NUMBER
    `in total`                                IS A NUMBER

-- cl 10(3)(a): actual loss of earnings, at the cl 9 rate, net of other payments (s 30(2)), limited to $20,000. Only
-- where the victim can demonstrate actual loss of earnings; otherwise (b) out-of-pocket expenses up to $5,000.
GIVEN `the weekly rate`        IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks`              IS A NUMBER
      `paid from another source` IS A NUMBER
      `the limit`              IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`actual loss of earnings at` `the weekly rate` `for` `the weeks` `less` `paid from another source` `within` `the limit` MEANS
    min `the limit` (max 0 ((`the weekly rate` TIMES `the weeks`) MINUS `paid from another source`))

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Primary victim claim`
GIVETH A `Financial assistance`
`the s 26 financial assistance for` `the claim` MEANS
    `Financial assistance` WITH
        `for immediate needs`                   IS `immediate needs`
        `for actual loss of earnings`           IS `earnings`
        `for out-of-pocket expenses`            IS `out of pocket`
        `for medical and dental expenses`       IS `medical`
        `for justice related expenses`          IS `justice`
        `for clothing and personal effects`     IS `clothing`
        `for economic loss, within the maximum` IS `economic loss`
        `taken off under s 26(2) or s 27(2)`    IS `the reduction`
        `in total`                              IS max 0 ((`immediate needs` PLUS `economic loss`) MINUS `the reduction`)
    WHERE
        `immediate needs` MEANS
            min `cl 10(1) -- maximum for a primary victim's immediate needs` (`the part not paid from another source` (`the claim`'s `immediate needs expenses`))
        `earnings` MEANS
            IF `the claim`'s `can demonstrate actual loss of earnings`
            THEN `actual loss of earnings at` (`the claim`'s `weekly rate of actual loss of earnings under cl 9`) `for` (`the claim`'s `weeks of actual loss of earnings`) `less` (`the claim`'s `lost earnings paid or payable from another source`) `within` `cl 10(3)(a) -- limit for actual loss of earnings`
            ELSE 0
        `out of pocket` MEANS
            IF `the claim`'s `can demonstrate actual loss of earnings`
            THEN 0
            ELSE min `cl 10(3)(b) -- limit for out-of-pocket expenses` (`the part not paid from another source` (`the claim`'s `out-of-pocket expenses`))
        `medical` MEANS
            `the part not paid from another source` (`the claim`'s `medical and dental expenses not claimed as immediate needs`)
        `justice` MEANS
            min `cl 10(3)(d) -- limit for justice related expenses` (`the part not paid from another source` (`the claim`'s `justice related expenses`))
        `clothing` MEANS
            min `cl 10(3)(e) -- limit for clothing and personal effects` (`the part not paid from another source` (`the claim`'s `clothing and personal effects`))
        `economic loss` MEANS
            min `cl 10(2) -- maximum for a primary victim's economic loss` (sum (LIST `earnings`, `out of pocket`, `medical`, `justice`, `clothing`))
        -- s 26(2): "Financial assistance for which a primary victim ... is eligible is reduced by the total amount paid
        -- or approved for payment to the victim's parent, step-parent or guardian under section 27". READING: the
        -- amount, not the maximum, is reduced (finding 8).
        `the reduction` MEANS
            `the claim`'s `paid or approved to the parent, step-parent or guardian under s 27`

§§ `s 27, Reg cl 11 -- a carer's financial assistance`

DECLARE `Carer claim` HAS
    -- cl 11(2)(a): "actual loss of earnings because of the need to care for the child as a direct result of the act".
    `can demonstrate actual loss of earnings`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `weekly rate of actual loss of earnings under cl 9`              IS A NUMBER
    `weeks of actual loss of earnings`                               IS A NUMBER
    `lost earnings paid or payable from another source`              IS A NUMBER
    `out-of-pocket expenses`                                         IS AN `Expense`
    -- cl 11(2)(c): "the actual medical and dental expenses of the child (other than expenses for which financial
    -- assistance for immediate needs is available for the child under section 26(1)(b))".
    `the child's medical and dental expenses not claimed as immediate needs` IS AN `Expense`
    `justice related expenses`                                       IS AN `Expense`
    -- cl 11(2)(e): clothing or personal effects "worn or carried by the primary victim".
    `the child's clothing and personal effects`                      IS AN `Expense`
    -- s 27(2).
    `paid or approved to the child under s 26(1)(c)`                 IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Carer claim`
GIVETH A `Financial assistance`
`the s 27 financial assistance for` `the claim` MEANS
    `Financial assistance` WITH
        `for immediate needs`                   IS 0
        `for actual loss of earnings`           IS `earnings`
        `for out-of-pocket expenses`            IS `out of pocket`
        `for medical and dental expenses`       IS `medical`
        `for justice related expenses`          IS `justice`
        `for clothing and personal effects`     IS `clothing`
        `for economic loss, within the maximum` IS `economic loss`
        `taken off under s 26(2) or s 27(2)`    IS `the reduction`
        `in total`                              IS max 0 (`economic loss` MINUS `the reduction`)
    WHERE
        `earnings` MEANS
            IF `the claim`'s `can demonstrate actual loss of earnings`
            THEN `actual loss of earnings at` (`the claim`'s `weekly rate of actual loss of earnings under cl 9`) `for` (`the claim`'s `weeks of actual loss of earnings`) `less` (`the claim`'s `lost earnings paid or payable from another source`) `within` `cl 11(2)(a) -- limit for a carer's actual loss of earnings`
            ELSE 0
        `out of pocket` MEANS
            IF `the claim`'s `can demonstrate actual loss of earnings`
            THEN 0
            ELSE min `cl 11(2)(b) -- limit for a carer's out-of-pocket expenses` (`the part not paid from another source` (`the claim`'s `out-of-pocket expenses`))
        `medical` MEANS
            `the part not paid from another source` (`the claim`'s `the child's medical and dental expenses not claimed as immediate needs`)
        `justice` MEANS
            min `cl 11(2)(d) -- limit for a carer's justice related expenses` (`the part not paid from another source` (`the claim`'s `justice related expenses`))
        `clothing` MEANS
            min `cl 11(2)(e) -- limit for the child's clothing and personal effects` (`the part not paid from another source` (`the claim`'s `the child's clothing and personal effects`))
        `economic loss` MEANS
            min `cl 11(1) -- maximum for a carer's economic loss` (sum (LIST `earnings`, `out of pocket`, `medical`, `justice`, `clothing`))
        -- s 27(2): "reduced by the total amount paid or approved for payment to the primary victim under section
        -- 26(1)(c)" (economic loss only; finding 8).
        `the reduction` MEANS
            `the claim`'s `paid or approved to the child under s 26(1)(c)`

-- Reg cl 9: the weekly rate is not covered. Where no actual loss of earnings can be demonstrated, cl 9 does not arise.
DECLARE `Weekly rate answer` IS ONE OF
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`
    `cl 9 does not arise: no actual loss of earnings is demonstrated, so out-of-pocket expenses are assessed instead (cl 10(3)(b), 11(2)(b))`

GIVEN `can demonstrate actual loss of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Weekly rate answer`
`the cl 9 weekly rate of actual loss of earnings` `can demonstrate actual loss of earnings` MEANS
    IF `can demonstrate actual loss of earnings`
    THEN `not covered` `the cl 9 rate: s 37 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987 as in force before the 2012 amendments, and its indexed amounts, are not deposited`
    ELSE `cl 9 does not arise: no actual loss of earnings is demonstrated, so out-of-pocket expenses are assessed instead (cl 10(3)(b), 11(2)(b))`

§§ `s 29, Reg cl 12 -- a family victim's financial support`

DECLARE `Family victim claim` HAS
    `immediate needs expenses`                                       IS AN `Expense`
    -- s 29(1)(b): "(less any amount payable under section 47)"; s 47(1)(b) clean-up expenses are immediate needs
    -- (Reg cl 13(a)).
    `amount payable under s 47 for clean-up, taken from immediate needs` IS A NUMBER
    -- s 29(1)(c): "funeral expenses actually incurred, or reasonably likely to be incurred, by the family victim for the
    -- funeral of the primary victim".
    `funeral expenses incurred or reasonably likely to be incurred`  IS A NUMBER
    -- s 29(2): "the total amount that may be granted for funeral expenses to all such family victims is the maximum
    -- amount prescribed by the regulations, less any amount payable under section 47".
    `funeral expenses already granted to other family victims`       IS A NUMBER
    `amount payable under s 47 for the funeral`                      IS A NUMBER
    -- s 29(1)(d) with cl 12(3): justice related expenses are the only economic loss the Regulation describes.
    `justice related expenses`                                       IS AN `Expense`

DECLARE `Family victim support` HAS
    `for the family victim's immediate needs`   IS A NUMBER
    `for the funeral`                           IS A NUMBER
    `for the family victim's justice related expenses` IS A NUMBER
    `in all`                                    IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Family victim claim`
GIVETH A `Family victim support`
`the s 29 financial support for` `the claim` MEANS
    `Family victim support` WITH
        `for the family victim's immediate needs`          IS `immediate needs`
        `for the funeral`                                  IS `funeral`
        `for the family victim's justice related expenses` IS `justice`
        `in all`                                           IS `immediate needs` PLUS `funeral` PLUS `justice`
    WHERE
        `immediate needs` MEANS
            min (max 0 (`cl 12(1) -- maximum for a family victim's immediate needs` MINUS `the claim`'s `amount payable under s 47 for clean-up, taken from immediate needs`))
                (`the part not paid from another source` (`the claim`'s `immediate needs expenses`))
        -- READING: s 30(2) speaks of "financial assistance"; a funeral payment is listed apart from it in s 18, so it
        -- is not reduced here (finding 10).
        `funeral` MEANS
            min (max 0 ((`cl 12(2) -- maximum for funeral expenses, in total` MINUS `the claim`'s `funeral expenses already granted to other family victims`) MINUS `the claim`'s `amount payable under s 47 for the funeral`))
                (`the claim`'s `funeral expenses incurred or reasonably likely to be incurred`)
        `justice` MEANS
            min `cl 12(3) -- maximum for a family victim's justice related expenses` (`the part not paid from another source` (`the claim`'s `justice related expenses`))

§§ `s 47, Reg cl 13 -- funeral and clean-up expenses of a person who is not a family victim`

-- s 47(1): applies to a person "who is not eligible for support in the form of financial assistance for immediate
-- needs or payment of funeral expenses under section 29 as a family victim", for "(a) expenses relating to the funeral
-- of a primary victim of an act of violence, (b) expenses associated with cleaning up damage caused to premises and
-- property as a direct result of an act of violence". (3): "an amount not exceeding the maximum amount in total
-- prescribed by the regulations and that the Commissioner considers to be fair and reasonable". (4)(a): it "is to be
-- paid from the amount ... for which the family victims are eligible under section 29".
DECLARE `Section 47 claim` HAS
    `is eligible for immediate needs or funeral expenses under s 29 as a family victim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `funeral expenses of the primary victim incurred`                                IS A NUMBER
    `clean-up expenses incurred`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `funeral expenses already granted to the family victims`                         IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Section 47 answer` IS ONE OF
    `s 47 does not apply: a family victim claims these expenses under s 29`
    `up to these amounts, as far as the Commissioner considers them fair and reasonable (s 47(3))` HAS
        `funeral reimbursement` IS A NUMBER
        `clean-up reimbursement` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Section 47 claim`
GIVETH A `Section 47 answer`
`the s 47 reimbursement for` `the claim` MEANS
    IF `the claim`'s `is eligible for immediate needs or funeral expenses under s 29 as a family victim`
    THEN `s 47 does not apply: a family victim claims these expenses under s 29`
    -- READING (finding 11): the s 47(4)(a) source caps the funeral payment at what is left of the one $9,500 total for
    -- all the family victims (s 29(2), cl 12(2)). The clean-up payment is capped by cl 13(a) alone: the immediate needs
    -- maximum is per family victim (cl 12(1)), and s 47(1)(b) needs no death, so there may be no family victim at all.
    -- s 29(1)(b) takes it off each family victim's immediate needs instead (the s 29 rule above).
    ELSE `up to these amounts, as far as the Commissioner considers them fair and reasonable (s 47(3))`
             (min (`the claim`'s `funeral expenses of the primary victim incurred`)
                  (max 0 (`cl 13(b) -- maximum for funeral expenses under s 47` MINUS `the claim`'s `funeral expenses already granted to the family victims`)))
             (min (`the claim`'s `clean-up expenses incurred`) `cl 13(a) -- maximum for immediate needs under s 47`)

§ `Part 4 Division 5 -- recognition payments (ss 34 to 36, s 53; Reg cl 14)`

-- s 34: "sexual assault has the meaning it has in paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (e) of the definition of sexual assault
-- and domestic violence in section 19(8)"; "sexual touching or sexual act" (Crimes Act 1900 Pt 3 Div 10); "series of
-- related acts has the same meaning as in section 19(4)". Homicide, serious bodily injury, offensive weapon, robbery,
-- assault and grievous bodily harm are borrowed terms, asked as facts (s 18 adds the destruction of a foetus to
-- grievous bodily harm).
DECLARE `Recognition facts` HAS
    `apparently occurred in the course of the commission of a homicide`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `involved a sexual assault`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sexual assault resulted in serious bodily injury`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sexual assault involved an offensive weapon`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sexual assault was carried out by 2 or more persons`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `involved sexual touching or a sexual act`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `involved an attempted sexual assault`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the attempted sexual assault involved violence`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the attempted sexual assault resulted in serious bodily injury`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `involved an assault`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the assault resulted in grievous bodily harm`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `involved physical assault of a child`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `involved a robbery involving violence`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 19(4)-(6), in the opinion of the Commissioner or Tribunal: a judgment, asked as a fact.
    `is one of a series of related acts`                                    IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Recognition category` IS ONE OF
    `category A (s 35(1))`
    `category B (s 35(2))`
    `category C (s 35(3))`
    `category D (s 35(4))`

-- s 35(1): "an act ... that apparently occurred in the course of the commission of a homicide".
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Recognition facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(1) describes` `the facts` IF
    `the facts`'s `apparently occurred in the course of the commission of a homicide`

-- s 35(2): "(a) a sexual assault resulting in serious bodily injury or which involved an offensive weapon or was
-- carried out by 2 or more persons, (b) a sexual assault, sexual touching or sexual act or attempted sexual assault
-- involving violence that is one of a series of related acts".
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Recognition facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(2) describes` `the facts` IF
        (    `the facts`'s `involved a sexual assault`
         AND (   `the facts`'s `the sexual assault resulted in serious bodily injury`
              OR `the facts`'s `the sexual assault involved an offensive weapon`
              OR `the facts`'s `the sexual assault was carried out by 2 or more persons`))
    OR  (    `the facts`'s `is one of a series of related acts`
         AND (   `the facts`'s `involved a sexual assault`
              OR `the facts`'s `involved sexual touching or a sexual act`
              OR (    `the facts`'s `involved an attempted sexual assault`
                  AND `the facts`'s `the attempted sexual assault involved violence`)))

-- s 35(3): "(a) a sexual assault other than one referred to in subsection (2)(b), (b) an attempted sexual assault
-- resulting in serious bodily injury, (c) an assault resulting in grievous bodily harm, (d) physical assault of a
-- child that is one of a series of related acts". A physical assault of a child is an assault.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Recognition facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(3) describes` `the facts` IF
        (`the facts`'s `involved a sexual assault` AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `is one of a series of related acts`)))
    OR  (`the facts`'s `involved an attempted sexual assault` AND `the facts`'s `the attempted sexual assault resulted in serious bodily injury`)
    OR  (    (`the facts`'s `involved an assault` OR `the facts`'s `involved physical assault of a child`)
         AND `the facts`'s `the assault resulted in grievous bodily harm`)
    OR  (`the facts`'s `involved physical assault of a child` AND `the facts`'s `is one of a series of related acts`)

-- s 35(4): "(a) sexual touching or sexual act, (b) an attempted sexual assault involving violence other than one
-- referred to in subsection (3)(b), (c) a robbery involving violence, (d) an assault (not resulting in grievous bodily
-- harm)".
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Recognition facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(4) describes` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `involved sexual touching or a sexual act`
    OR  (    `the facts`'s `involved an attempted sexual assault`
         AND `the facts`'s `the attempted sexual assault involved violence`
         AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `the attempted sexual assault resulted in serious bodily injury`)))
    OR  `the facts`'s `involved a robbery involving violence`
    OR  (    (`the facts`'s `involved an assault` OR `the facts`'s `involved physical assault of a child`)
         AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `the assault resulted in grievous bodily harm`)))

-- The categories overlap (finding 12): every category whose description fits, in order.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Recognition facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Recognition category`
`the categories describing` `the facts` MEANS
    concat (LIST (IF `s 35(1) describes` `the facts` THEN LIST `category A (s 35(1))` ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF `s 35(2) describes` `the facts` THEN LIST `category B (s 35(2))` ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF `s 35(3) describes` `the facts` THEN LIST `category C (s 35(3))` ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF `s 35(4) describes` `the facts` THEN LIST `category D (s 35(4))` ELSE EMPTY))

-- The person to whom a recognition payment may be payable.
DECLARE `Recognition recipient` HAS
    -- s 36(1)(c)-(e): "a primary victim who suffered injury as a result of" the act. A seat sets it from
    -- `is a primary victim of` (s 20), never from the injury facts alone (finding 25).
    `is a primary victim who suffered injury`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 36(1)(a), (b): the family of a primary victim who died.
    `relationship to the primary victim who died`                                   IS A `Relationship to the person who died`
    `had cohabited with the primary victim for at least 2 years`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 36(1)(a)(i), (b): "immediately before the death ... was financially dependent on the primary victim".
    `was financially dependent on the primary victim immediately before the death`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 36(1)(a)(ii): "each child of a primary victim who, immediately before the death ..., was under the age of 18".
    `was under 18 immediately before the death`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 29(4)(b): "a child of the primary victim born after the death of the victim where, had the child been born in
    -- the victim's lifetime, the child would have been a financially dependent family member".
    `was born after the death and would have been financially dependent`            IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 36(2): "Only one recognition payment is payable to a single victim in respect of a series of related acts".
    `has been given a recognition payment for another act in the same series`       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 19(6): "An act is not related to any earlier act in respect of which support is given under this Act if it
    -- occurs after the support is given."
    `the act occurred after support was given for the earlier act`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 53: "an application to the Tribunal for an administrative review of a decision concerning a recognition
    -- payment suspends the application of section 16 in relation to the payment", "Subject to any order of the
    -- Tribunal to the contrary".
    `has applied to the Tribunal for review of a decision about the recognition payment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Tribunal has ordered that the payment is not suspended`                    IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Category A recipient` IS ONE OF
    `s 36(1)(a): a financially dependent family victim, or a child under 18`
    `s 29(3), (4)(b) with s 36(1)(a): a child born after the death who would have been financially dependent`
    `s 36(1)(b): a parent, step-parent, guardian, spouse or de facto partner who was not financially dependent`
    `not a person to whom s 36(1)(a) or (b) pays category A`

-- s 36(1)(a)(i): "each family victim (other than a child referred to in subparagraph (ii)) who ... was financially
-- dependent"; (ii): each child under 18; (b): those not financially dependent who were "(i) a parent, step-parent or
-- guardian of the primary victim, (ii) ... the victim's spouse or de facto partner as referred to in section 22(3)(b)".
GIVEN `the recipient` IS A `Recognition recipient`
GIVETH A `Category A recipient`
`the category A recipient class of` `the recipient` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF      `is a member of the immediate family (s 22(3))` (`the recipient`'s `relationship to the primary victim who died`) (`the recipient`'s `had cohabited with the primary victim for at least 2 years`)
            AND `the recipient`'s `was financially dependent on the primary victim immediately before the death`
        THEN `s 36(1)(a): a financially dependent family victim, or a child under 18`
        IF      `the recipient`'s `relationship to the primary victim who died` EQUALS `child`
            AND `the recipient`'s `was under 18 immediately before the death`
        THEN `s 36(1)(a): a financially dependent family victim, or a child under 18`
        IF      `the recipient`'s `relationship to the primary victim who died` EQUALS `child`
            AND `the recipient`'s `was born after the death and would have been financially dependent`
        THEN `s 29(3), (4)(b) with s 36(1)(a): a child born after the death who would have been financially dependent`
        IF      `the recipient`'s `relationship to the primary victim who died` EQUALS `parent, guardian or step-parent`
            OR  `the recipient`'s `relationship to the primary victim who died` EQUALS `spouse`
            OR  (    `the recipient`'s `relationship to the primary victim who died` EQUALS `de facto partner`
                 AND `the recipient`'s `had cohabited with the primary victim for at least 2 years`)
        THEN `s 36(1)(b): a parent, step-parent, guardian, spouse or de facto partner who was not financially dependent`
        OTHERWISE `not a person to whom s 36(1)(a) or (b) pays category A`

GIVEN `the class` IS A `Category A recipient`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the category A amount for` `the class` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `s 36(1)(b): a parent, step-parent, guardian, spouse or de facto partner who was not financially dependent` THEN `cl 14(b) -- category A under s 36(1)(b)`
    WHEN `not a person to whom s 36(1)(a) or (b) pays category A` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE `cl 14(a) -- category A under s 36(1)(a)`

GIVEN `the category` IS A `Recognition category`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cl 14 amount for` `the category` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the category`
    WHEN `category B (s 35(2))` THEN `cl 14(c) -- category B`
    WHEN `category C (s 35(3))` THEN `cl 14(d) -- category C`
    WHEN `category D (s 35(4))` THEN `cl 14(e) -- category D`
    WHEN `category A (s 35(1))` THEN `cl 14(a) -- category A under s 36(1)(a)`

DECLARE `Why no recognition payment` IS ONE OF
    `no category in s 35 describes the act`
    `only one recognition payment is payable for a series of related acts against the victim (s 36(2))`
    `the act is category A, which s 36(1)(a) and (b) pay only to listed members of the family of the primary victim who died`
    `categories B, C and D are payable only to a primary victim who suffered injury (s 36(1)(c) to (e))`
    `a recognition payment is given only in respect of an act of violence or act of modern slavery (ss 35, 36(1)); a road crime alone gives its family victims counselling only (s 29A)`

DECLARE `Recognition answer` IS ONE OF
    `a recognition payment` HAS
        `the category`         IS A `Recognition category`
        `the amount in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `a recognition payment, suspended pending the Tribunal's review (s 53)` HAS
        `the suspended category`        IS A `Recognition category`
        `the suspended amount in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no recognition payment` HAS `why` IS A `Why no recognition payment`

-- s 36(1)(c)-(e): a primary victim who suffered injury is paid the category B, C or D that describes the act.
-- READING: where more than one does, the highest (finding 12). Category A is never payable to a primary victim.
GIVEN `the categories` IS A LIST OF `Recognition category`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Recognition category`
`the highest of categories B to D in` `the categories` MEANS
    IF elem `category B (s 35(2))` `the categories` THEN JUST `category B (s 35(2))`
    ELSE IF elem `category C (s 35(3))` `the categories` THEN JUST `category C (s 35(3))`
         ELSE IF elem `category D (s 35(4))` `the categories` THEN JUST `category D (s 35(4))`
              ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A `Recognition recipient`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 36(2) rules out a further payment to` `the recipient` IF
        `the recipient`'s `has been given a recognition payment for another act in the same series`
    AND (NOT (`the recipient`'s `the act occurred after support was given for the earlier act`))

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A `Recognition recipient`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recognition payment is suspended for` `the recipient` IF
        `the recipient`'s `has applied to the Tribunal for review of a decision about the recognition payment`
    AND (NOT (`the recipient`'s `the Tribunal has ordered that the payment is not suspended`))

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A `Recognition recipient`
      `the category`  IS A `Recognition category`
      `the amount`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Recognition answer`
`the payment to` `the recipient` `of` `the category` `at` `the amount` MEANS
    IF `the recognition payment is suspended for` `the recipient`
    THEN `a recognition payment, suspended pending the Tribunal's review (s 53)` `the category` `the amount`
    ELSE `a recognition payment` `the category` `the amount`

-- s 36: the payments payable to the recipient for the act. Category A to listed family, then the best of B to D to an
-- injured primary victim; a person can be both (finding 13).
GIVEN `the facts`     IS A `Recognition facts`
      `the recipient` IS A `Recognition recipient`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Recognition answer`
`the recognition payments for` `the facts` `to` `the recipient` MEANS
    IF null `the categories`
    THEN LIST (`no recognition payment` `no category in s 35 describes the act`)
    ELSE IF `s 36(2) rules out a further payment to` `the recipient`
         THEN LIST (`no recognition payment` `only one recognition payment is payable for a series of related acts against the victim (s 36(2))`)
         ELSE IF null `the payments`
              THEN LIST (`no recognition payment` `the reason there is none`)
              ELSE `the payments`
    WHERE
        `the categories` MEANS `the categories describing` `the facts`
        `the category A payment` MEANS
            IF      elem `category A (s 35(1))` `the categories`
                AND `the category A amount for` (`the category A recipient class of` `the recipient`) GREATER THAN 0
            THEN LIST (`the payment to` `the recipient` `of` `category A (s 35(1))` `at` (`the category A amount for` (`the category A recipient class of` `the recipient`)))
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the primary victim payment` MEANS
            IF `the recipient`'s `is a primary victim who suffered injury`
            THEN CONSIDER `the highest of categories B to D in` `the categories`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
                 WHEN JUST `c` THEN LIST (`the payment to` `the recipient` `of` `c` `at` (`the cl 14 amount for` `c`))
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the payments` MEANS append `the category A payment` `the primary victim payment`
        `the reason there is none` MEANS
            IF elem `category A (s 35(1))` `the categories`
            THEN `the act is category A, which s 36(1)(a) and (b) pay only to listed members of the family of the primary victim who died`
            ELSE `categories B, C and D are payable only to a primary victim who suffered injury (s 36(1)(c) to (e))`

-- s 35(1)-(4): each category "is a payment given in respect of an act of violence or act of modern slavery", and
-- s 36(1)(a)-(e) pay each for "an act of violence or act of modern slavery described in section 35". So the act must
-- be one of those. A road crime is not an act of violence (s 19(3A)), except in the s 25(2A), (2B) circumstances, and
-- its family victims get counselling only (s 29A) (finding 25).
GIVEN `the act`       IS A `The act`
      `the facts`     IS A `Recognition facts`
      `the recipient` IS A `Recognition recipient`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Recognition answer`
`the s 36 recognition payments for` `the act` `the facts` `the recipient` MEANS
    IF (`is an act of violence` `the act` OR `is an act of modern slavery` `the act`)
    THEN `the recognition payments for` `the facts` `to` `the recipient`
    ELSE LIST (`no recognition payment` `a recognition payment is given only in respect of an act of violence or act of modern slavery (ss 35, 36(1)); a road crime alone gives its family victims counselling only (s 29A)`)

§ `Part 4 Division 4 -- approved counselling services (ss 31 to 33; Reg cl 5 to 8)`

-- Reg cl 4: "victim" means a family victim, a primary or secondary victim, or a "relevant family member" (a relative
-- of a primary victim who died, or of a person killed in a road crime, who is not a family victim).
DECLARE `Counselling class` IS ONE OF
    `a primary or secondary victim`
    `a family victim`
    `a relevant family member: a relative of a person who died who is not a family victim`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `Counselling facts` HAS
    `counselling class`                                                       IS A `Counselling class`
    -- cl 5(3): an initial 2 hours "if satisfied that counselling may assist in establishing whether or not the person
    -- is a victim".
    `whether the person is a victim is still being established`               IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 5(5): "If counselling services are provided for a victim outside of Australia".
    `the counselling is provided outside Australia`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the counsellor's hourly fee outside Australia`                           IS A NUMBER
    -- cl 7: "(a) a person under the age of 18 years who is a victim of sexual assault or physical abuse, or (b) a person
    -- who, while under the age of 18 years, was a victim of sexual assault or physical abuse".
    `is, or was while under 18, a victim of sexual assault or physical abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 5(1): the limits apply "to each act"; s 30A: counselling once for the act.
    `hours of counselling already paid for the act`                           IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Counselling answer` IS ONE OF
    `no approved counselling services under the Scheme`
    `an initial 2 hours of counselling, while the Commissioner establishes whether the person is a victim (cl 5(3))`
    `counselling on an ongoing basis, if the Commissioner authorises it (cl 7)`
    `up to this many more hours, and further periods if the Commissioner considers it appropriate; more than 22 hours in all only for exceptional reasons (cl 5(2), (4))` HAS
        `hours for a primary or secondary victim` IS A NUMBER
    `up to this many more hours, and a further period if requested (cl 5(7))` HAS
        `hours for a family victim` IS A NUMBER
    `if the Commissioner considers it appropriate, up to this many more hours, and a further period if requested (cl 5(6), (7))` HAS
        `hours for a relevant family member` IS A NUMBER
    `outside Australia, up to this many more hours, and no more than this many more dollars (cl 5(5))` HAS
        `hours outside Australia`   IS A NUMBER
        `dollars outside Australia` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Counselling facts`
GIVETH A `Counselling answer`
`the counselling hours for` `the facts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `whether the person is a victim is still being established`
        THEN `an initial 2 hours of counselling, while the Commissioner establishes whether the person is a victim (cl 5(3))`
        IF `the facts`'s `counselling class` EQUALS `none of these`
        THEN `no approved counselling services under the Scheme`
        IF `the facts`'s `is, or was while under 18, a victim of sexual assault or physical abuse`
        THEN `counselling on an ongoing basis, if the Commissioner authorises it (cl 7)`
        IF `the facts`'s `the counselling is provided outside Australia`
        THEN `outside Australia, up to this many more hours, and no more than this many more dollars (cl 5(5))` `the hours left abroad` `the dollars left abroad`
        IF `the facts`'s `counselling class` EQUALS `a family victim`
        THEN `up to this many more hours, and a further period if requested (cl 5(7))` `the hours left`
        IF `the facts`'s `counselling class` EQUALS `a relevant family member: a relative of a person who died who is not a family victim`
        THEN `if the Commissioner considers it appropriate, up to this many more hours, and a further period if requested (cl 5(6), (7))` `the hours left`
        OTHERWISE `up to this many more hours, and further periods if the Commissioner considers it appropriate; more than 22 hours in all only for exceptional reasons (cl 5(2), (4))` `the hours left`
    WHERE
        `the hours left` MEANS max 0 (`cl 5(2) -- hours of counselling` MINUS `the facts`'s `hours of counselling already paid for the act`)
        `the fee` MEANS `the facts`'s `the counsellor's hourly fee outside Australia`
        -- cl 5(5): "not more than a total of 22 hours or a maximum of $5,500, whichever is the lesser".
        `the dollar limit abroad` MEANS min (`cl 5(2) -- hours of counselling` TIMES `the fee`) `cl 5(5) -- dollar limit for counselling outside Australia`
        `the dollars left abroad` MEANS
            IF `the fee` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN max 0 (`the dollar limit abroad` MINUS (`the facts`'s `hours of counselling already paid for the act` TIMES `the fee`))
            ELSE `cl 5(5) -- dollar limit for counselling outside Australia`
        `the hours left abroad` MEANS
            IF `the fee` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN `the dollars left abroad` DIVIDED BY `the fee`
            ELSE `the hours left`

-- Reg cl 8 Table: "1 Generalist counsellors tier 1 $120 per hour; 2 Generalist counsellors tier 2 $144 per hour;
-- 3 Psychiatrists $256 per hour". Who is tier 2 (cl 4) is asked as a fact, because its last limb is the
-- Commissioner's opinion: "(a) is a registered psychologist or is eligible for membership of the Australian
-- Association of Social Workers (other than as a student member), and (b) has provided ... approved counselling
-- services under the Act for more than 3 consecutive years, and (c) holds post-graduate qualifications consisting of a
-- Masters degree (or a higher level qualification) in social work, clinical psychology, clinical neuropsychology,
-- counselling psychology or forensic psychology, and (d) has, in the opinion of the Commissioner, specialist
-- counselling skills". Tier 1 is any other counsellor the Commissioner approves under s 31 (finding 26).
DECLARE `Counsellor class` IS ONE OF
    `a generalist counsellor tier 1`
    `a generalist counsellor tier 2`
    `a psychiatrist`

GIVEN `the counsellor` IS A `Counsellor class`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cl 8 hourly rate for` `the counsellor` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the counsellor`
    WHEN `a generalist counsellor tier 1` THEN 120
    WHEN `a generalist counsellor tier 2` THEN 144
    WHEN `a psychiatrist` THEN 256

DECLARE `Counselling services` HAS
    `the counsellor`                                   IS A `Counsellor class`
    `hours of counselling`                             IS A NUMBER
    -- cl 8(2): "Any period of more than 2 hours during which a counsellor travels to provide approved counselling
    -- services to a victim is to be counted".
    `hours of the counsellor's travel period`          IS A NUMBER
    -- cl 8(1)(b), (3): GST payable, not more than 10% of the (1)(a) amount.
    `GST payable`                                      IS A NUMBER
    -- cl 8(1)(c): "the amount, determined by the Commissioner, to be appropriate to cover costs".
    `costs the Commissioner determines to be appropriate` IS A NUMBER
    -- cl 8(1): "provided to a victim who is resident in Australia"; otherwise cl 5(10).
    `the victim is resident in Australia`              IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Counselling payment answer` IS ONE OF
    `the payment for the counselling is` HAS `counselling dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `paid on an invoice, statement or other document, in the manner the Commissioner approves (cl 5(10)): the cl 8 scale is for victims resident in Australia`

-- READING: a travel period of more than 2 hours counts in full; one of 2 hours or less does not count (finding 15).
GIVEN `the services` IS A `Counselling services`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the hours counted under cl 8` `the services` MEANS
    `the services`'s `hours of counselling` PLUS
        (IF `the services`'s `hours of the counsellor's travel period` GREATER THAN `cl 8(2) -- travel period that counts, more than this many hours`
         THEN `the services`'s `hours of the counsellor's travel period`
         ELSE 0)

GIVEN `the services` IS A `Counselling services`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cl 8(1)(a) scale amount for` `the services` MEANS
    `the cl 8 hourly rate for` (`the services`'s `the counsellor`) TIMES `the hours counted under cl 8` `the services`

GIVEN `the services` IS A `Counselling services`
GIVETH A `Counselling payment answer`
`the cl 8 payment for` `the services` MEANS
    IF `the services`'s `the victim is resident in Australia`
    THEN `the payment for the counselling is`
             (`the scale amount`
              PLUS min (`the services`'s `GST payable`) (`the scale amount` TIMES `cl 8(3) -- GST cap, as a share of the scale amount`)
              PLUS `the services`'s `costs the Commissioner determines to be appropriate`)
    ELSE `paid on an invoice, statement or other document, in the manner the Commissioner approves (cl 5(10)): the cl 8 scale is for victims resident in Australia`
    WHERE
        `the scale amount` MEANS `the cl 8(1)(a) scale amount for` `the services`

§ `Part 4 Division 6 -- applications (ss 38 to 40)`

§§ `s 38 -- who may apply`

-- s 38(1): "(a) a victim of an act of violence or act of modern slavery, (a1) a family victim of a road crime, (b) a
-- parent, step-parent or guardian of a primary victim who is a child, (c) any other person, on behalf of a victim, who
-- has a genuine interest in the welfare of that victim."
DECLARE `Capacity of the applicant` IS ONE OF
    `a victim of an act of violence or an act of modern slavery`
    `a family victim of a road crime`
    `a parent, step-parent or guardian of a primary victim who is a child`
    `another person with a genuine interest in the victim's welfare, applying on the victim's behalf`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `the capacity` IS A `Capacity of the applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply for victims support as` `the capacity` IF
    NOT (`the capacity` EQUALS `none of these`)

§§ `s 39 -- documentary evidence`

DECLARE `Kind of support applied for` IS ONE OF
    `approved counselling services`
    `financial assistance for immediate needs`
    `financial assistance for actual loss of earnings`
    `financial assistance for out-of-pocket expenses (cl 10(3)(b))`
    `financial assistance for medical and dental expenses`
    `financial assistance for justice related expenses (cl 10(3)(d))`
    `financial assistance for clothing and personal effects`
    `funeral expenses`
    `a recognition payment`

DECLARE `Evidence facts` HAS
    `kind of support`                                                   IS A `Kind of support applied for`
    `applying as`                                                       IS A `Victim class`
    `has a police report`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 39(2)(b)(i), (5): "a Government agency or any other agency that provides support services to victims of
    -- crime", including a non-government agency funded by the Commonwealth or the State.
    `has a report by a government agency or a victims support agency`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a medical, dental or counselling report verifying the injury`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 39(4)(a): "receipts, invoices or other approved forms of substantiation".
    `has receipts, invoices or other substantiation of the expenses`    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 39(4)(b): "the name and address of the employer, the period of absence from work and a statement from the
    -- employer substantiating those particulars".
    `has the employer's details and statement of the period off work`   IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Missing evidence` IS ONE OF
    `documentary evidence, such as a medical or police report or a victims support agency's report, supporting the claim to be a victim (s 39(2)(a))`
    `a police report, or a report by a government agency or a victims support agency (s 39(2)(b)(i))`
    `a medical, dental or counselling report verifying the injury (s 39(2)(b)(ii))`
    `receipts, invoices or other approved substantiation of the expenses (s 39(4)(a))`
    `the employer's name and address, the period of absence from work and the employer's statement (s 39(4)(b))`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of support applied for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is economic loss` `the kind` IF
        `the kind` EQUALS `financial assistance for actual loss of earnings`
    OR  `the kind` EQUALS `financial assistance for out-of-pocket expenses (cl 10(3)(b))`
    OR  `the kind` EQUALS `financial assistance for medical and dental expenses`
    OR  `the kind` EQUALS `financial assistance for justice related expenses (cl 10(3)(d))`
    OR  `the kind` EQUALS `financial assistance for clothing and personal effects`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of support applied for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is for actual expenses` `the kind` IF
        `the kind` EQUALS `financial assistance for immediate needs`
    OR  `the kind` EQUALS `financial assistance for out-of-pocket expenses (cl 10(3)(b))`
    OR  `the kind` EQUALS `financial assistance for medical and dental expenses`
    OR  `the kind` EQUALS `financial assistance for justice related expenses (cl 10(3)(d))`
    OR  `the kind` EQUALS `financial assistance for clothing and personal effects`
    OR  `the kind` EQUALS `funeral expenses`

-- s 39(2)(a): "for an application for financial assistance for immediate needs under section 26"; (b): "for an
-- application for financial assistance for economic loss under section 26 or 27 or for a recognition payment".
GIVEN `the facts` IS AN `Evidence facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Missing evidence`
`the evidence s 39 asks for that is missing` `the facts` MEANS
    concat (LIST (IF `needs (2)(a)` AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `has a police report` OR `the facts`'s `has a report by a government agency or a victims support agency` OR `the facts`'s `has a medical, dental or counselling report verifying the injury`))
                  THEN LIST `documentary evidence, such as a medical or police report or a victims support agency's report, supporting the claim to be a victim (s 39(2)(a))`
                  ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF `needs (2)(b)` AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `has a police report` OR `the facts`'s `has a report by a government agency or a victims support agency`))
                  THEN LIST `a police report, or a report by a government agency or a victims support agency (s 39(2)(b)(i))`
                  ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF `needs (2)(b)` AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `has a medical, dental or counselling report verifying the injury`))
                  THEN LIST `a medical, dental or counselling report verifying the injury (s 39(2)(b)(ii))`
                  ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF `is for actual expenses` (`the facts`'s `kind of support`) AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `has receipts, invoices or other substantiation of the expenses`))
                  THEN LIST `receipts, invoices or other approved substantiation of the expenses (s 39(4)(a))`
                  ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF `the facts`'s `kind of support` EQUALS `financial assistance for actual loss of earnings` AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `has the employer's details and statement of the period off work`))
                  THEN LIST `the employer's name and address, the period of absence from work and the employer's statement (s 39(4)(b))`
                  ELSE EMPTY))
    WHERE
        `under s 26 or 27` MEANS
                `the facts`'s `applying as` EQUALS `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)`
            OR  `the facts`'s `applying as` EQUALS `a parent, step-parent or guardian caring for a child primary victim (s 23(2), s 27)`
        `needs (2)(a)` MEANS
                `the facts`'s `kind of support` EQUALS `financial assistance for immediate needs`
            AND `the facts`'s `applying as` EQUALS `a primary victim (s 23(1), s 26)`
        `needs (2)(b)` MEANS
                (`is economic loss` (`the facts`'s `kind of support`) AND `under s 26 or 27`)
            OR  `the facts`'s `kind of support` EQUALS `a recognition payment`

§§ `s 40 -- time for making, and duration of, applications`

DECLARE `Application timing` HAS
    `kind of support`                                                          IS A `Kind of support applied for`
    `the victim's date of birth`                                               IS A DATE
    -- READING: for a series of related acts the Act does not say which act the period runs from (finding 16).
    `the day the act occurred`                                                 IS A DATE
    -- s 40(2): a family victim, where "it was only established ... that the primary victim died as a direct result of
    -- the relevant act of violence subsequently to the occurrence".
    `is a family victim, and the cause of death was only established later`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day it was established that the death was a direct result of the act` IS A DATE
    -- s 40(5): "involving domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault" (undefined there: finding 17).
    `the act involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault`        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 40(7): "a person who is a primary victim of an act of violence that occurs in the course of the commission of a
    -- sexual offence against the person when the person is under 18 years of age".
    `is a primary victim of an act of violence in the course of a sexual offence against them` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Time limit rule` IS ONE OF
    `s 40(1): 2 years after the act`
    `s 40(1): 2 years after the victim turns 18`
    `s 40(3): 2 years after it was established that the primary victim died as a direct result of the act`
    `s 40(5): 10 years after the act`
    `s 40(5): 10 years after the victim turns 18`

DECLARE `Time limit answer` IS ONE OF
    `no time limit: s 40 applies only to applications for financial support or a recognition payment`
    `no time limit: s 40(7), for a child victim of a sexual offence`
    `apply on or before` HAS
        `the last day` IS A DATE
        `under`        IS A `Time limit rule`

GIVEN `the timing` IS AN `Application timing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the victim was a child when the act occurred` `the timing` IF
    `was a child on` (`the timing`'s `the victim's date of birth`) (`the timing`'s `the day the act occurred`)

-- s 40(7): "This section (other than subsection (6)) does not apply to an application for financial support, being for
-- financial assistance of a kind specified in the Victims Rights and Support Regulation 2019, clause 10(3)(b) or (d), or
-- a recognition payment for" a child victim of a sexual offence. "There is no time limit".
GIVEN `the timing` IS AN `Application timing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 40(7) takes the time limit away for` `the timing` IF
        `the timing`'s `is a primary victim of an act of violence in the course of a sexual offence against them`
    AND `the victim was a child when the act occurred` `the timing`
    AND (   `the timing`'s `kind of support` EQUALS `financial assistance for out-of-pocket expenses (cl 10(3)(b))`
         OR `the timing`'s `kind of support` EQUALS `financial assistance for justice related expenses (cl 10(3)(d))`
         OR `the timing`'s `kind of support` EQUALS `a recognition payment`)

-- s 40(1) or (5): the period from the act, or from the day a child victim turns 18.
GIVEN `the timing` IS AN `Application timing`
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`the s 40(1) or (5) last day for` `the timing` MEANS
    IF      `the timing`'s `kind of support` EQUALS `a recognition payment`
        AND `the timing`'s `the act involved domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault`
    THEN IF `the victim was a child when the act occurred` `the timing`
         THEN `apply on or before` (`s 40(5) -- years to apply for a recognition payment` `years after` (`the day the person turns 18` (`the timing`'s `the victim's date of birth`))) `s 40(5): 10 years after the victim turns 18`
         ELSE `apply on or before` (`s 40(5) -- years to apply for a recognition payment` `years after` (`the timing`'s `the day the act occurred`)) `s 40(5): 10 years after the act`
    ELSE IF `the victim was a child when the act occurred` `the timing`
         THEN `apply on or before` (`s 40(1) -- years to apply` `years after` (`the day the person turns 18` (`the timing`'s `the victim's date of birth`))) `s 40(1): 2 years after the victim turns 18`
         ELSE `apply on or before` (`s 40(1) -- years to apply` `years after` (`the timing`'s `the day the act occurred`)) `s 40(1): 2 years after the act`

-- s 40(2), (3): a family victim may apply "within 2 years after it is established that the primary victim died as a
-- direct result". READING: whichever of that day and the s 40(1) or (5) day is later (finding 16).
GIVEN `the timing` IS AN `Application timing`
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`the time limit for` `the timing` MEANS
    IF `the timing`'s `kind of support` EQUALS `approved counselling services`
    THEN `no time limit: s 40 applies only to applications for financial support or a recognition payment`
    ELSE IF `s 40(7) takes the time limit away for` `the timing`
         THEN `no time limit: s 40(7), for a child victim of a sexual offence`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the s 40(1) or (5) last day for` `the timing`
              WHEN `apply on or before` `the day` `the rule` THEN
                  IF      `the timing`'s `is a family victim, and the cause of death was only established later`
                      AND `is on or before` `the day` `the s 40(3) day`
                      AND (NOT (`the day` EQUALS `the s 40(3) day`))
                  THEN `apply on or before` `the s 40(3) day` `s 40(3): 2 years after it was established that the primary victim died as a direct result of the act`
                  ELSE `apply on or before` `the day` `the rule`
              OTHERWISE `the s 40(1) or (5) last day for` `the timing`
    WHERE
        `the s 40(3) day` MEANS `s 40(3) -- years to apply after the cause of death is established` `years after` (`the timing`'s `the day it was established that the death was a direct result of the act`)

-- Whether an application made on a day is in time.
GIVEN `the day made` IS A DATE
      `the timing`   IS AN `Application timing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an application made on` `the day made` `is in time for` `the timing` IF
    CONSIDER `the time limit for` `the timing`
    WHEN `apply on or before` `the last day` `the rule` THEN `is on or before` `the day made` `the last day`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The days from the act to the last day, for the regulative rule (NOTHING: no time limit).
GIVEN `the timing` IS AN `Application timing`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the days from the act to the last day to apply for` `the timing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the time limit for` `the timing`
    WHEN `apply on or before` `the last day` `the rule` THEN JUST (`the days from` (`the timing`'s `the day the act occurred`) `to` `the last day`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 40(6): "Claims may continue to be made under an application that is duly made ... until whichever of the following
-- first occurs-- (a) the expiration of the period of 5 years after the application is made, (b) the total maximum
-- amount of financial support that the victim is eligible to receive under this Act in respect of that act ... has
-- been given."
DECLARE `Claims answer` IS ONE OF
    `claims may be made under the application up to and including` HAS `the last day for claims` IS A DATE
    `no further claims: 5 years have passed since the application was made (s 40(6)(a))`
    `no further claims: the total maximum amount of financial support has been given (s 40(6)(b))`

GIVEN `the day the application was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for claims under an application made on` `the day the application was made` MEANS
    `s 40(6)(a) -- years in which claims may be made under an application` `years after` `the day the application was made`

GIVEN `the day the application was made`    IS A DATE
      `the day of the claim`                IS A DATE
      `the total maximum has been given`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Claims answer`
`whether claims may be made under an application made on` `the day the application was made` `on` `the day of the claim` `when` `the total maximum has been given` MEANS
    IF `the total maximum has been given`
    THEN `no further claims: the total maximum amount of financial support has been given (s 40(6)(b))`
    ELSE IF `is on or before` `the day of the claim` (`the last day for claims under an application made on` `the day the application was made`)
         THEN `claims may be made under the application up to and including` (`the last day for claims under an application made on` `the day the application was made`)
         ELSE `no further claims: 5 years have passed since the application was made (s 40(6)(a))`

§ `Regulative rules -- the applicant and the Commissioner`

-- Clock: days. For s 40 the clock starts on the day of the act; for s 40(6) on the day the application is made.
DECLARE `VRSA party` IS ONE OF `the applicant`, `the Commissioner`

DECLARE `VRSA act` IS ONE OF
    `duly make the application for financial support or a recognition payment`
    `determine the application and give the applicant written notice`
    `make a claim under the application`
    `pay the amount claimed, subject to the conditions of the approval`

-- s 43(1): "After considering an application for victims support, the Commissioner must determine the application--
-- (a) by approving the giving of the victims support, or (b) by dismissing the application." (4): "Written notice is
-- to be given to the applicant". No period is stated: the obligation never becomes a breach by time alone.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VRSA party` `VRSA act`
DECIDE `s 43 -- the Commissioner must determine a duly made application and give written notice` IS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST  `determine the application and give the applicant written notice`

-- s 40(1): "an application for financial support or a recognition payment must be duly made within 2 years after the
-- relevant act of violence occurred or, if the victim was a child ..., within 2 years after the day on which the child
-- concerned turns 18"; (3), (5): the longer periods; (7): no time limit. The Act gives no power to extend. A BREACH
-- here means the time to apply has passed, not an offence.
GIVEN `days from the act to the last day` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VRSA party` `VRSA act`
DECIDE `s 40 -- the application must be duly made in time` IS
    CONSIDER `days from the act to the last day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        PARTY `the applicant`
        MUST  `duly make the application for financial support or a recognition payment`
        HENCE `s 43 -- the Commissioner must determine a duly made application and give written notice`
    WHEN JUST `the days` THEN
        PARTY  `the applicant`
        MUST   `duly make the application for financial support or a recognition payment`
        WITHIN `the days`
        HENCE  `s 43 -- the Commissioner must determine a duly made application and give written notice`
        LEST   BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 40: the application for financial support or a recognition payment was not duly made within the time allowed (2 years after the act or after a child victim turns 18; 10 years for a recognition payment involving domestic violence, child abuse or sexual assault; 2 years after a later-established cause of death), and the Act gives no power to extend it"

-- s 54(2): "On receiving the application for payment, the Commissioner must (subject to the conditions of the approval
-- and any deductions made in accordance with those conditions) pay the relevant amount". No period is stated.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VRSA party` `VRSA act`
DECIDE `s 54(2) -- the Commissioner must pay a claim under an approved application` IS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST  `pay the amount claimed, subject to the conditions of the approval`

-- s 40(6): claims "may continue to be made" until 5 years after the application or the total maximum is given; after
-- that, no claim may be made under it. Making a claim is a choice (DO); one claim is traced from the start.
GIVEN `days left in the 5 years after the application` IS A NUMBER
      `the total maximum has been given`              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VRSA party` `VRSA act`
DECIDE `s 40(6) -- claims under a duly made application, for 5 years or until the maximum is given` IS
    IF `the total maximum has been given`
    THEN PARTY `the applicant`
         SHANT `make a claim under the application`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 40(6)(b): the total maximum amount of financial support has been given, so no further claim can be made under the application"
    ELSE PARTY  `the applicant`
         DO     `make a claim under the application`
         WITHIN `days left in the 5 years after the application`
         HENCE  `s 54(2) -- the Commissioner must pay a claim under an approved application`
         LEST
             PARTY `the applicant`
             SHANT `make a claim under the application`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 40(6)(a): 5 years have passed since the application was made, so no further claim can be made under it"
